.TH CCOL_CHAN_ENABLE_SENDING 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_enable_sending \- enable sending on a ccol_channel direction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_chan_enable_sending(ccol_channel *ch, ccol_channel_direction d);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Re-enables send operations on the specified direction that were previously
disabled and wakes all threads currently blocked waiting to send.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to modify
d    Direction to enable (ccol_owner_to_workers or ccol_workers_to_owner)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - Sending enabled successfully
ccol_invalid_args  - ch is NULL or d is invalid
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Wakes all blocked senders via broadcast
Threads can immediately attempt to send if space is available
Does not affect the opposite direction
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_disable_sending (3)
